# SABOTAGE: T77 (spec §I4 "unfair advantage") — REGENERATED T160 (context shifted: the
# billing_factor cond now dispatches on `scoring_status`, and T160 P3/P5 added a
# cancelled/inactive-aware cond shape around this clause — the DUNNING clause itself is
# unchanged). Health-formula integrity: removes the
# `dunning?(scoring_status, pd) -> {dunning_value(pd), dunning_explanation(scoring_status,
# pd)}` clause from `Samen.Web.AccountHealth`'s billing factor `cond`. Without it, a book
# with ANY number of past-due subscriptions/invoices, at ANY overdue age, falls straight
# through to the `scoring_status in [:active, :trialing] -> {1.0, ...}` branch — the exact
# health/dunning incoherence `Samen.Web.Operator.HealthScore` (WS-B/ADR-019) was built to
# fix, reintroduced independently in this module's own (deliberately separate) formula. A
# book in deep dunning (max-cap-eligible: 90+ days overdue) would score a PERFECT billing
# dimension (1.0) and the composite would read "healthy" instead of "at risk" — precisely
# the lie a health score exists to prevent, AND (fix round 1) the same bug the WORST-OF-N
# fix closed at the status-selection layer would be reopened at the SCORING layer even with
# the correct worst status selected. This clause serves BOTH the per-account path
# (`scoring_status` defaults to the plain worst-of-N `subscription_status` when T160's
# `:scoring_status` key is absent) and the portfolio path — dropping it breaks dunning
# scoring on both. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_account_health_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: score/1: DUNNING CEILING caps the billing value even at max cap-eligible overdue age
# MUST_FAIL: snapshot/2: DUNNING wiring — a real past-due invoice caps the billing dimension end-to-end
# MUST_FAIL: snapshot/2 WORST-OF-N (fix round 1, MED-2): an active sub + a sibling past_due sub reports the WORST status, never the best one
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
@@ -459,9 +459,6 @@
         scoring_status in [:cancelled, :canceled] ->
           {0.0, "at least one customer subscription is cancelled — treat as churn risk in this book"}
 
-        dunning?(scoring_status, pd) ->
-          {dunning_value(pd), dunning_explanation(scoring_status, pd)}
-
         scoring_status in [:active, :trialing] ->
           {1.0, active_explanation(scoring_status, cancelled_count)}
 
